-- A correction of fx_stats, no change in play: 360 stats on 3433 lines were marked as read by nothing, and code does
-- read them. The first sort of the stats only looked for a stat's constant; these are read another way:
--   239 through a name the code builds at run time (added damage by type and bound, leech by damage type and pool,
--      damage returned to attackers by type, "damage can / cannot chill" by type and ailment, added damage by weapon
--      kind, damage over time multipliers by ailment, a golem kind's buff effect, an aura's "reserves no mana", the
--      Heist enchantment magnitudes by modifier kind);
--   29 "Minions ..." stats: a minion is given every minion_ stat of its owner under the plain name, and these are
--      the ones whose plain name monster code reads;
--   92 by a name written out in the code as text.
-- Plain "Adds # to # Cold Damage" is among them: hits already count it for attacks and spells alike
-- (DamageStats.RawAdded), as the real game does.
